1
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:51,000
The enemy isn't out there... it is within.

2
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Recon is a war, thriller film directed by Robert Port.

3
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Four American soldiers in WW2, after witnessing the vicious murder of an innocent civilian at the hands of
their platoon Sergeant, are sent on a reconnaissance/suicide mission led by a local partisan.

4
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Marson, played by Alexander Ludwig.

5
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:51,000
Heisman, played by RJ Fetherstonhaugh.

6
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Hopewell, played by Mitch Ainley.

7
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:21,000
Asch, played by Chris Brochu.

8
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Walberg, played by Christopher Crema.

9
00:42:45,000 --> 00:42:51,000
Angelo, played by Franco Nero.

10
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:36,000
Tom Clancy's Ghost Recon is a series of military tactical
shooter video games published by Ubisoft.

11
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:21,000
In the series, the player is in charge of a
fictional, newly conceived squad of U.S.

12
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Army Special Forces soldiers from Delta Company, 1st Battalion, 5th
Special Forces Group (5th SFG) stationed at Fort Bragg.

13
01:01:45,000 --> 01:01:51,000
Except for the "1st Battalion, 5th SFG" designation, this reconnaissance unit is entirely fictional,
as Special Forces Battalions currently only support three Companies (A, B and C).

14
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:36,000
They are often referred to as "the Ghosts".

15
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
Their role is like other real world special operations forces, in
that their operations are kept highly classified.

16
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
In Tom Clancy's Ghost Recon: Future Soldier, it is shown that the Ghost's unit has multiple designations and is part of JSOC; they are also known as the Group for
Specialized Tactics (or GST—where the term "Ghost" comes from), much like real JSOC units such as Delta Force (1st SFOD-D or CAG) and SEAL Team Six (or DEVGRU).

17
01:20:45,000 --> 01:20:51,000
Tom Clancy's Ghost Recon has also been novelized by Grant
Blackwood under the pseudonym David Michaels.

18
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
As of 2025, over 40 million units have been sold.

19
01:30:15,000 --> 01:30:21,000
The tone is intense.
